UObjectToolTips.TimelineEffectContext:
Custom FGameplayEffectContext subclass for timeline ability elements.

Carries additional data that the standard effect context doesn't support:
- AttachSocketName: Which socket on the avatar to attach VFX/SFX to.
- InstanceID:       Unique ID for multi-instance cue tracking. Allows multiple
                    simultaneous looping cues (particles/sounds) on the same actor
                    to be spawned and removed independently.
- bIsRemoval:       When true, signals the GC notify to destroy the instance
                    identified by InstanceID rather than spawn a new one.

This travels through the GAS replication path (NetSerialize) so GC notifies
on simulated proxies can read the socket, asset, and instance data without
any float hacks.

Usage:
  FTimelineEffectContext* Ctx = new FTimelineEffectContext();
  Ctx->AddInstigator(AvatarActor, nullptr);
  Ctx->AddSourceObject(ParticleAsset);
  Ctx->AttachSocketName = FName("RightHand");
  Ctx->InstanceID = GenerateTimelineCueInstanceID();
  FGameplayEffectContextHandle Handle(Ctx);

